text:
maria: Quick follow-up from the RFC review — we still need to pick the concrete interface between ingress (api-gateway) and quota/fair-scheduler. do we expose a per-request lease with optional token accounting, or keep it coarse-grained (request-only) and let backend do the per-token split?

ajit: leaning toward per-request lease with optional token hints. simpler for gateway, lets scheduler make smarter batching decisions. downside is more churn in scheduler.

leah: +1 for token hints. most of latency/cost decisions depend on tokens. We can keep hints optional for older clients.

kai: curious about semantics — if gateway sends token_hint=500 but actual tokens=50, how do we reconcile? capacity should be reclaimed. need clear contract: unused lease tokens go back to pool.

maria: good point. proposal: lease has {units_allocated, units_used, release(reason)}. release triggers async reclaim. can we make reclaim idempotent?

ajit: yes, reclaim idempotent. also add a ttl on leases so leaked ones auto-expire.

leah: what about fairness? we talked about per-customer weighted shares. scheduler needs both outstanding leases and real usage to adjust. token_hint helps. but if hints are optional, worst-case we get blind fairness.

kai: tradeoff: requiring token hints forces gateway to run cheap token counters (estimates). that is extra work but it's local and fast. optional hints lower rollout friction. maybe require hints for dedicated/dedicated-v2 tenants and optional for hosted?

maria: operationally that maps to tiers — agree. We also need the API surface. sketch:

```proto
message LeaseRequest {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string route_id = 2;
  int64 units_hint = 3; // optional token estimate
  int64 timeout_ms = 4;
}
message LeaseResponse {
  string lease_id = 1;
  int64 units_allocated = 2;
  int64 expires_at_ms = 3;
}
message LeaseRelease {
  string lease_id = 1;
  int64 units_used = 2;
  string reason = 3;
}
```

leah: API looks fine. add field in LeaseResponse: fallback_policy enum (allow, queue, deny) so gateway can decide immediately.

maria: yes — fallback_policy is important. default for hosted is queue-with-timeout. dedicated default is allow-with-billing.

dave: how about interop with existing rate-cap tokens we have in ingress? we can't rip-and-replace. need a shim adapter that maps old counters to lease requests. shim can be a sidecar or library.

kai: +1 for shim. prefer library for gateway (node/go SDK) and sidecar for legacy infra. SDKs emit units_hint based on request content.

leah: observability: emit span tags: lease.id, units.requested, units.allocated, units.used, policy. also new metric: lease.leak_reclaim_count. dashboards and alerts.

ops-bot: deploy: quota-service/v2 built and smoke tests passed on staging (ci/2345) :white_check_mark:

maria: rollout plan idea:
- alpha: internal tenants + dedicated-v2, require hints
- beta: hosted opt-in (gateway sends hints when present)
- GA: hosted requires hints for heavy routes (>10r/s) or falls back to coarse-grain mode

ajit: tests: unit tests for reclaim, ttl expiry, idempotent release; integration tests: end-to-end with shim and gateway; chaos: simulate lost release (ensure ttl reclaim) and overestimate/underestimate patterns.

kai: one more edge: model-calling flows where a single API call fans out to multiple internal model requests. gateway should allocate for the whole workflow or per-leg? I'd prefer allocate at ingress for total expected tokens, but we need a helper in SDK to add child leases.

maria: agreed. include child_lease links in LeaseResponse and allow hierarchical release. helps routing and billing.

leah: can we enforce a max over-allocation factor (e.g., 2x hint) to avoid someone gaming the system?

ajit: yes, scheduler should have configurable max_allocation_ratio per-tenant and global hard cap.

maria: action items:
- ajit: draft proto + error codes and fallback enum (due EOD Wed)
- kai: prototype gateway SDK emitting units_hint (early integration)
- leah: metrics/dashboards spec + alert thresholds
- dave: shim adapter spec for legacy ingress

maria: we'll sync Fri 11am to lock the interface. thanks all :rocket:
